text.section:
The notice of a hearing when mailed to any person, as provided in § 46.2-402 shall contain:

A specific statement of the alleged offense or offenses or other grounds for suspension or revocation of the license, including the date, time and place thereof when applicable;


The date, time and place of the hearing;


The names and addresses of all known witnesses whose testimony is proposed to be taken at the hearing;


As to any record of conviction of any offense which is to be offered as evidence, the date of the conviction and the court in which the same was had.
